COMMUNITY MEETING

Place: #openvpn-discussion on irc.freenode.net
Date: Thursday, 11th January 2010
Time: 19:00 UTC

Full log available here:

http://secure-computing.net/logs/%23%23openvpn-discussion.log

Next meeting on Thu 18th Feb 2010. Same place, same time.

SUMMARY

New developments were summarized by mattock. A few community site forum software choices here:

- http://www.secure-computing.net/wiki/index.php/User:Mattock

Initial, very incomplete developer documentation is available:

- http://www.secure-computing.net/wiki/index.php/OpenVPN/Developer_documentation

These IRC meeting logs are linked to from here: 

- http://www.secure-computing.net/wiki/index.php/OpenVPN/IRC_meetings

The OpenVPN Git "testing" tree(s)/branch(es) are hosted in "openvpn" project in SF.net. Dazo was granted developer access. Instructions for it's use are available in the above developer documentation.

Discussed mailing list <-> forum integration in some length. In the light of new findings it may not be worth it trying to integrate them after all. However, syncing mailing lists to a read-only forums would be useful when searching for information. Mattock will take a closer look at this issue.

Packaging the "testing" version of OpenVPN for various OS'es was also discussed in some length. Ecrist can help getting "testing" to freebsd-devel ports tree.

